From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:34:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: measure pipeline library link time against fast
 linking

VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library expects a link that omits
VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_LINK_TIME_OPTIMIZATION_BIT_EXT to be cheap next to building
the libraries it links, and
dEQP-VK.pipeline.pipeline_library.graphics_library.misc.other.compare_link_times
warns when a link costs more than ten times the creation of the two libraries
carrying its shaders.  KosmicKrisp answers graphicsPipelineLibraryFastLinking
with false and the conformance test warns, so record what the driver actually
spends and pin the one promise it does make.

The new kosmickrisp_pipeline_library_link_time test builds the same eight
libraries the conformance test builds - two vertex-input, two
pre-rasterization with a specialized vertex shader, two fragment-shader with a
specialized fragment shader and two fragment-output - links all sixteen
combinations and reports every link against the creation of the libraries that
carry its shaders.  On an M1 Ultra a library costs 0.001 to 0.296 ms, because
deferring a stage only serializes its NIR, while a link costs 0.46 to 0.72 ms
once Metal has the stage's MSL text in its compiled-source cache and 11.5 to
14.6 ms when it does not; the first link of a process pays about 60 ms more
still.  The conformance test randomizes its specialization constants, so the
five or six links that first meet a distinct MSL text pay the cold price and
exceed the ratio.

Linking is the first moment either stage can be compiled at all.  Metal builds
an MTLLibrary from the whole MSL text of a stage and an MTLRenderPipelineState
from the functions of every stage at once, and has no object that holds one
separately compiled stage for a later link.  Nor is a stage's text known
earlier: Metal has no fixed-function vertex fetch, so kk_lower_vs_vbo builds
the attribute loads into the vertex shader from the vertex-input state, and
kk_lower_fs_blend builds the blend, the write mask and the logic op into the
fragment shader from the colour-blend state - each owned by a library other
than the one holding the shader.  Compiling on first draw would only move the
same work into rendering, which is the stall the extension exists to avoid.

The test therefore fails only when a driver advertises fast linking it does
not deliver, which keeps the false answer honest and turns the timing into a
requirement the day the answer becomes true.
